  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "38fd3d2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Business scenario\n",
    "\n",
    "##### Assume the company has a normal individual-purchase limit:\n",
    "\n",
    "### A single customer order should not have an average order value above $5,000. High-value purchases above this limit are expected to involve multiple orders rather than one unusually expensive order."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "0920b88d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "suspect = (\n",
    "    (df['avg_order_value_usd'] > 5000) &\n",
    "    (df['total_orders'] == 1)\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "d7e54d35",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def get_iqr(column):\n",
    "    Q1 = df[column].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "    Q3 = df[column].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    IQR = Q3 - Q1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    lower_bound = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR\n",
    "    upper_bound = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"IQR:\", IQR)\n",
    "    print(\"Lower bound:\", lower_bound)\n",
    "    print(\"Upper bound:\", upper_bound)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return IQR, lower_bound, upper_bound"
   ]
  },
